    "terrainName": "farm",
    "description": "What: a flock betrays an ambush (CE-4623 AB-5 / AB-8; docs/designs/animals/DESIGN_Animals.md \u00a75 / \u00a79). On the farm terrain the 'Orchard birds' area (36 x 36 m at (240, 120)) holds one perched, singing flock of 20. A three-man ambush party ('Ambusher 1'..'3', Hostile) walks from (290, 172) through the orchard to an ambush spot at its south edge (\u2248 (225, 100)); a three-man patrol ('Patrol 1'..'3', Friend) walks east along y = 78 (north of the pasture fence) from x 40. The men in the orchard are inside the birds' flight zone: the flock lifts off and the birdsong stops BEFORE any shot is fired, and the alarm call reaches the patrol's ears. Judge: (1) the flock is perched at the start (2) the flock lifts off (3) the birdsong stops (the flock is frightened) (4) both happen before the first shot (5) a patrol man hears it before the first shot. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh ua-animal-flock-flush"
  },
